    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p71-q84-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "starts at $(0,8)$ and stops at $(-4,0)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "One suitable parametrisation is $P(t)=(-t,8-2t)$, $0\\leq t\\leq4$, with $t$ in seconds.",
          "worked": "Choose $x=-t$. On the supplied segment,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2x+8\\\\y&=8-2t.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $t=0$, $P=(0,8)$; at $t=4$, $P=(-4,0)$. For $0<t<4$, the point lies between the endpoints. Thus $P(t)=(-t,8-2t)$ for $0\\leq t\\leq4$ seconds is suitable.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p71-q84-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "moves from $(-4,0)$ to $(0,8)$, and back to $(-4,0)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "One suitable parametrisation is $P(t)=(-2-2\\cos t,4-4\\cos t)$, $0\\leq t\\leq2\\pi$, with $t$ in seconds and cosine arguments in radians.\n\nUse one cosine cycle to traverse the segment and return.",
          "worked": "Choose $x=-2-2\\cos t$, so $-4\\leq x\\leq0$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2x+8\\\\y&=2(-2-2\\cos t)+8\\\\y&=4-4\\cos t.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $t=0$, $P=(-4,0)$; at $t=\\pi$, $P=(0,8)$; at $t=2\\pi$, $P=(-4,0)$. At $t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$, $P=(-2,4)$. Cosine decreases on $[0,\\pi]$ and increases on $[\\pi,2\\pi]$, giving the required outward and return motion. Restrict $0\\leq t\\leq2\\pi$ seconds.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p71-q84-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "starts at $(-4,0)$ and stops at $(0,8)$ in 2 seconds.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(t)=(-4+2t,4t)$, $0\\leq t\\leq2$, with $t$ in seconds.",
          "worked": "A uniform traversal in 2 seconds has coordinate rates\n$$\\begin{align*}v_x&=\\frac{0-(-4)}{2}=2\\\\v_y&=\\frac{8-0}{2}=4.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $P(t)=(-4+2t,4t)$ for $0\\leq t\\leq2$ seconds. The endpoints are $P(0)=(-4,0)$ and $P(2)=(0,8)$; $P(1)=(-2,4)$ lies between them.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
